<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements Tuesday, the New York Fed said.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters had expected the Fed to remain out of the system after adding reserves with three-day fixed-system repurchase agreements Monday, as well as a coupon pass.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at the official target of 5.25 percent.</p>
<p>((--John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663))</p>
